            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+system"} epi-mono factorization
          %p
            There is a trade-off here. As you allow more sophisticated language, you widen the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theories"} theories
            that can be expressed, but you narrow the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            in which it makes sense to take
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theories"} theories
            containing the ones you are interested in. For example, you
            %em could
            treat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            as an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+algebraic+theory"} essentially algebraic theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            with
            %em all
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            would do.
          %p
            Before I get onto
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/properties"} properties
            that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            are assumed to have, you can also alter the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            with which they are equipped.
          %p
            Take
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+monoids"} internal monoids
            in any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
            can be regarded as the free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            containing an
            = succeed "." do
