                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f = \left ( P \rightarrowtail R \times R \stackrel{\mathrm{pr}_{1}}{\to } R \right ).
          %p
            We can talk about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/images"} images
            in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            factorizes essentially uniquely as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epi"} epi
            followed by a mono. So, define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↣
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \rightarrowtail R
            by the factorization
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
