          %p
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epi"} epi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +
          %p
            If you have read Section 
            %a{:href => "#sectionb"}> 2
            , you will recognize that the informal talk of ‘
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"}> sets
            ’ (really,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
